Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The anchored rebuild ops asked for after reverting f057ddd (86554f5).

Two causes, both closed here:
- The guard fired on any reply that sounded like a deletion, so a plain
  question ("Who do I have as a lawyer?") could get [Yes, delete it]. It now
  fires only when the owner's own line asked to delete / forget / remove.
- The wider word list matched inside other words: "quit[ée]" inside "quite",
  "elimin[ée]" inside "eliminate". Every claim word is now matched whole,
  with "no letter before / after" edges that work for Georgian and Cyrillic
  too (\b knows only Latin), and Spanish takes only the accented past
  ("borré"), never "borre", which is also "that I delete".

Tests: ordinary replies with "quite", "eliminate", "quitar", "borre",
„ამოვიღეთ" and "удалился" claim nothing; the 3302 claims still do.

DONE WHEN: SE-042 step 1 and PR-019 step 2 run 5 times each on fresh seats
with no delete card, and ME-016 / PR-036 (incl. „მოვხსენი") still pass.

